    "41": {
      "key": [],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "[MVU]变量更新格式",
      "content": "【Rakudai Kishi · Variable Output Format】\nThis entry defines the output structure only. Follow [MVU]变量更新规则 for field permissions, update conditions, and scoring. Read actual previous values from the current branch state provided by [MVU]变量列表.\n\n【Placement and Structure】\nEnd the narrative with exactly one literal <UpdateVariable> block: <Analysis> followed by <JSONPatch>, with all closing tags.\nAnalysis: briefly state confirmed updates and needed roster corrections in English. For scores, give actual old value, change, and final value; distinguish any first-assessment baseline. Omit unchanged characters and long reasoning.\nJSONPatch: a valid JSON array, with actual operations for every needed update. No code fences, separate patch heading, comments, ellipses, or placeholders. Use literal tags without backslashes. Apply the per-person check in [MVU]变量更新规则; describing a correction does not save it, and submitting it does not prove runtime success.\n\n【Paths and Operations】\nThe variable container is stat_data. Patch paths begin with /系统, /玩家, /场景, or /人际. Do not prepend /stat_data.\n- replace: Update an existing writable path. Include op, path, and value. The value must be the final value, not the change amount.\n- add: Create a missing entry or optional field. Include op, path, and value; create missing parents first. For existing people, patch only the relevant child fields, preserving the rest of the object.\n- remove: Use only for corrective deletions permitted by the update rules. Include op and path; omit value.\nUse only this card’s defined fields and data types. An empty string means unspecified, null means unknown, an empty collection means no records, and booleans must be true/false. These are not interchangeable. Write numbers as JSON numbers, and booleans as native JSON booleans (true/false) without quotes or numbers (not \"true\" or 1/0). Names must be non-empty, must not contain / or ~, and must not be __proto__, prototype, or constructor.\n\n【Ability Records】\n/玩家/伐刀能力/招式/<Name> and /玩家/其他能力/<Name> must use an object containing only 说明 (string), 条件与代价 (string), and 掌握状态 (待确认, 学习中, or 已掌握). For new entries, use \"\" for unspecified text and 待确认 for an unconfirmed status. Update existing abilities through their specific child fields, preserving other values. Write 学习中 or 已掌握 explicitly only when supported by confirmed learning results; compatibility handling never infers mastery from description text.\n\n【Event Records】\n/场景/已发生事件 is an object keyed by stable event names. Each event contains 卷号 (a JSON integer from 1 to 19; write 1 for 第一卷, never \"第一卷\" or \"1\"), 章段 (the exact stable string key from the currently injected chapter directory), 结果 (non-empty text describing the actual result in one or two sentences), 参与者 (an array of names), and 知情者 (an array of names). Follow the update rules for valid progress and who actually knows the result.\n\n【Optional Schedule and Roster Fields】\n/场景/日程 is an optional object keyed by stable schedule names. Each schedule object contains exactly these required fields: 类型 (比赛, 训练, 约定, or 其他), 日期 (an empty string or a valid calendar date in YYYY-MM-DD form), 时间 (string), 地点 (string), 参与者 (array of strings), 状态 (待定, 已安排, 进行中, 已完成, or 已取消), and 说明 (string). Follow [MVU]变量更新规则 for when each field may change.\nWhen /场景/日程 is absent, place an add operation creating that parent object with value {} before operations adding its children. When the parent exists, address only the relevant entry or field; do not replace the entire schedule object. The same parent-before-child order applies to other optional objects.\n/人际/<Name>/名册隐藏 is an optional native JSON boolean reserved for terminal user actions. Do not output operations that add, modify, or remove it, including through a parent-object replacement or deletion. Omit this field when creating a relationship entry.\n/系统/已删除人物 is an optional array of names managed only by the terminal's permanent-removal action. It belongs to the current message and active swipe, not the entire chat. Do not modify it or recreate its listed relationship entries from earlier messages; existing event references to those names remain valid. On rollback, use only the selected branch snapshot.\n\n【First-encounter Roster Entries】\nFollow [MVU]变量更新规则 for registration, interaction, and scoring decisions. New /人际/<Name> objects require 关系, 态度印象, 好感, 支援度, 羁绊阶段, 变化依据. For an ordinary new person with no score change, use 好感:0, 支援度:0, 羁绊阶段:未建立, 变化依据:\"\". For actual changes, write the final score and its evidence. Established special relationships retain their one-time background assessment under the update rules; do not give them the ordinary zero default.\n- 联系状态: exactly 仅识别 or 已建立联系. This records reciprocal interaction, NOT exchanged contact details. The first mutual conversation or directed action qualifies under the update rules.\n- 联系依据: a string identifying both sides' actions; non-empty for 已建立联系, \"\" for 仅识别. Update a stale 关系 label in the same patch. These fields record interaction; they do not gate scoring or automatically grant affection.\n- 已加联系方式: an independent boolean for an available messaging/phone channel. A face-to-face conversation alone does not set it true; preserve an existing true.\n- 性别: 未知, 男性, or 女性. 已知资料: an object with string children 身份, 登记等级, 灵装, 已知能力. Put confirmed facts here even if already stated in 态度印象; omit unknowns.\nOrdinary first scores use 0 plus the current justified change, with no fixed 50 bonus. Existing numbers continue from their actual value; old null may use zero for current changes, but unreadable/missing old values may not. Write new 变化依据 before numerical updates and 好感突破依据 for major changes as required by the update rules. Existing characters need only changed or confirmed missing child fields, including contact facts from earlier in the current branch. Create a missing 已知资料 parent with {} before its children. Preserve unrelated data and scores; do not recreate permanently removed people or infer unknown facts. Write all needed corrections in JSONPatch, not only Analysis.\n\n【Format When Nothing Changes】\nUse [] only when there are no confirmed changes or missing roster facts to submit; otherwise write the required operations:\n<UpdateVariable>\n<Analysis>No confirmed variable changes occurred this turn.</Analysis>\n<JSONPatch>\n[]\n</JSONPatch>\n</UpdateVariable>\n",
